IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sgta-nouns`

-- Telecommunications Act 1999 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (TA1999.txt).
-- PART 1: s 2 Interpretation -- the definitions that the Tier 1 provisions use.
-- Each definition is a function of facts a witness could state (see sgta-nouns.l4).
-- Seat layer, tests and the answer to any question about a person are elsewhere; this module says only what
-- the definitions say.
--
-- FORK 1 (recorded in TV-QUESTION.md section 4; NOTES.md points there): the Act has NO definition of "radio-communication equipment".
-- It has "equipment" (an appliance, apparatus or accessory used or intended to be used for telecommunications)
-- and "radio-communication" (any telecommunication by means of Hertzian or radio waves).
-- This module composes the two, word for word: equipment used or intended to be used for a telecommunication that
-- is by means of Hertzian or radio waves.  That composition is a reading, not a defined term.

§ `s 2 Interpretation`

-- src:529 | “telecommunications” means a transmission, emission or
-- src:530 | reception of signs, signals, writing, images, sounds or
-- src:531 | intelligence of any nature by wire, radio, optical or other
-- src:532 | electromagnetic systems whether or not such signs, signals,
-- src:533 | writing, images, sounds or intelligence have been subjected
-- src:534 | to re‑arrangement, computation or other processes by any
-- src:535 | means in the course of their transmission, emission or
-- src:536 | reception;
@ref s 2 "telecommunications" (src:529-536)
GIVEN e IS A `A piece of equipment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2: the equipment is used or intended to be used for telecommunications` MEANS
        (NOT (null (e's `acts it is used or intended to be used for`)))
    AND (NOT (null (e's `means it uses`)))

-- src:325 | “equipment” includes any appliance, apparatus or accessory
-- src:326 | used or intended to be used for telecommunications,
-- src:327 | including (to avoid doubt) any such appliance, apparatus or
-- src:328 | accessory capable of being used for the operation of any
-- src:329 | broadcasting service;
@ref s 2 "equipment" (src:325-329)
GIVEN e IS A `A piece of equipment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2: this is equipment` MEANS
    `s 2: the equipment is used or intended to be used for telecommunications` e

-- src:331 | “Hertzian or radio waves” means electromagnetic waves of
-- src:332 | frequencies not exceeding 1,000 terahertz propagated in
-- src:333 | space without any artificial guide;
@ref s 2 "Hertzian or radio waves" (src:331-333)
GIVEN `frequency in terahertz` IS A NUMBER
      `propagated in space without any artificial guide` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2: these are Hertzian or radio waves` MEANS
        `frequency in terahertz` AT MOST 1000
    AND `propagated in space without any artificial guide`

-- src:450 | “radio-communication” means any telecommunication by
-- src:451 | means of Hertzian or radio waves;
@ref s 2 "radio-communication" (src:450-451)
GIVEN `means used` IS A `Means of telecommunication`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2: the means used is radio-communication` MEANS
    `means used` EQUALS `Hertzian or radio waves`

-- FORK 1: composed from "equipment" and "radio-communication"; there is no defined term.
-- src:325 | “equipment” includes any appliance, apparatus or accessory
-- src:326 | used or intended to be used for telecommunications,
-- src:327 | including (to avoid doubt) any such appliance, apparatus or
-- src:328 | accessory capable of being used for the operation of any
-- src:329 | broadcasting service;
-- src:450 | “radio-communication” means any telecommunication by
-- src:451 | means of Hertzian or radio waves;
@ref s 2 "equipment" (src:325-329); "radio-communication" (src:450-451)
GIVEN e IS A `A piece of equipment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2 (composed): the equipment is radio-communication equipment` MEANS
        `s 2: this is equipment` e
    AND elem `Hertzian or radio waves` (e's `means it uses`)

-- src:344 | “message” means any sign, signal, writing, image, sound,
-- src:345 | intelligence or information of any nature transmitted by
-- src:346 | telecommunications;
@ref s 2 "message" (src:344-346)
GIVEN `what is sent` IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`s 2: the message` MEANS `what is sent`

-- src:270 | “Authority” means the Info‑communications Media
-- src:271 | Development Authority established by section 3 of the
-- src:272 | Info‑communications Media Development Authority
-- src:273 | Act 2016;
@ref s 2 "Authority" (src:270-273)
GIVEN `the body` IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2: this body is the Authority` MEANS
    `the body` EQUALS "Info-communications Media Development Authority"

-- src:275 | “broadcasting apparatus” and “broadcasting service” have the
-- src:276 | meanings given by the Broadcasting Act 1994;
@ref s 2 "broadcasting apparatus" and "broadcasting service" (src:275-276)
GIVEN `has the meaning the Broadcasting Act 1994 gives broadcasting apparatus` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2: this is broadcasting apparatus (the Broadcasting Act's meaning, supplied)` MEANS
    `has the meaning the Broadcasting Act 1994 gives broadcasting apparatus`

-- src:516 | “telecommunication service” means any service for
-- src:517 | telecommunications, including the leasing of a
-- src:518 | telecommunication cable, but excludes any broadcasting
-- src:519 | service;
@ref s 2 "telecommunication service" (src:516-519)
GIVEN `is a service for telecommunications` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is a broadcasting service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2: this is a telecommunication service` MEANS
        `is a service for telecommunications`
    AND (NOT `is a broadcasting service`)

-- src:521 | “telecommunication system” means any system used or
-- src:522 | intended to be used for telecommunications, including (to
-- src:523 | avoid doubt) any such system capable of being used for the
-- src:524 | operation of any broadcasting service;
@ref s 2 "telecommunication system" (src:521-524)
GIVEN `is used or intended to be used for telecommunications` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is capable of being used for the operation of a broadcasting service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2: this is a telecommunication system` MEANS
        `is used or intended to be used for telecommunications`
    OR (`is capable of being used for the operation of a broadcasting service` AND `is used or intended to be used for telecommunications`)

-- src:507 | “telecommunication licensee” means a person to whom a
-- src:508 | licence has been granted under section 5 or 7;
@ref s 2 "telecommunication licensee" (src:507-508)
GIVEN `holds a licence granted under section 5` IS A BOOLEAN
      `holds a licence granted under section 7` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2: this person is a telecommunication licensee` MEANS
    `holds a licence granted under section 5` OR `holds a licence granted under section 7`

-- src:526 | “telecommunication system licensee” means a person licensed
-- src:527 | under section 5 to operate a telecommunication system;
@ref s 2 "telecommunication system licensee" (src:526-527)
GIVEN `is licensed under section 5 to operate a telecommunication system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2: this person is a telecommunication system licensee` MEANS
    `is licensed under section 5 to operate a telecommunication system`

-- src:439 | “public telecommunication licensee” means a person designated
-- src:440 | by the Authority under section 8;
@ref s 2 "public telecommunication licensee" (src:439-440)
GIVEN `designated by the Authority under section 8` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2: this person is a public telecommunication licensee` MEANS
    `designated by the Authority under section 8`

-- src:453 | “radio-communication service” means any service for
-- src:454 | radio‑communications;
@ref s 2 "radio-communication service" (src:453-454)
GIVEN `is a service for radio-communications` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2: this is a radio-communication service` MEANS
    `is a service for radio-communications`

-- src:456 | “radio-communication system” means any system used or
-- src:457 | intended to be used for radio‑communications;
@ref s 2 "radio-communication system" (src:456-457)
GIVEN `is a system used or intended to be used for radio-communications` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2: this is a radio-communication system` MEANS
    `is a system used or intended to be used for radio-communications`

-- src:552 | “vessel” includes any ship, boat, air‑cushioned vehicle or
-- src:553 | floating rig or platform used in any form of operations at
-- src:554 | sea or any other description of vessel.
@ref s 2 "vessel" (src:552-554)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of craft`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2: this is a vessel` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `not a vessel` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- src:459 | “repealed Act” means the Telecommunication Authority of
-- src:460 | Singapore Act (Cap. 323, 1993 Revised Edition) repealed by
-- src:461 | the Info‑communications Development Authority of
-- src:462 | Singapore Act (Cap. 137A, 2000 Revised Edition);
@ref s 2 "repealed Act" (src:459-462)
GIVEN `name of the Act` IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2: this is the repealed Act` MEANS
    `name of the Act` EQUALS "Telecommunication Authority of Singapore Act (Cap. 323, 1993 Revised Edition)"

-- src:484 | “TAS” means the Telecommunication Authority of Singapore
-- src:485 | reconstituted by the repealed Act;
@ref s 2 "TAS" (src:484-485)
GIVEN `name of the body` IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2: this body is TAS` MEANS
    `name of the body` EQUALS "Telecommunication Authority of Singapore"
